Adapted components:

- `tools/review_gate.py`   — cross-model-family review verdict transition table
- `tools/run_state.py`     — multi-stage run state machine (done vs accepted);
  also inlines the model-family mapping table from ARIS `tools/provenance.py`
- `tools/iteration_log.py` — per-round iteration / staleness tracker
- `tools/watchdog.py`      — heartbeat staleness detector
- `mcp-servers/codex-exec/`    — Codex CLI reviewer bridge (MCP over stdio)
- `mcp-servers/manual-review/` — human-relay reviewer bridge
- `mcp-servers/feishu-bridge/` — Feishu/Lark notification & approval bridge
- `mcp-servers/llm-chat/`    — OpenAI-compatible HTTP reviewer bridge
- `skills/shared-references/`  — gate / contract / resumability doctrine
  (rewritten and condensed for the general-programming domain)

The orchestration skeleton (startup authorization block, per-round loop,
failure-signature triage, evidence-level verification, HANDOFF protocol,
5-line morning summary) is generalized from the `night-auto-work` skill
by the AWIS project author.
